    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0322" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg216"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1906-08-09">August 9,
                        1906</date>.</hi></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 370.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In further reference to the economic policy
                    of Japan in Manchuria and especially to my dispatch No. 364 of July 31, I
                    inclose herewith an abstract of an interview given by the Japanese minister of
                    foreign affairs to a representative of one of the leading Japanese papers on
                    this subject.</p>
                <p>Viscount Hayashi’s statements are, you will note, in absolute agreement with
                    those which have at various times been made to me by Japanese officials or
                    foreigners in whose opinions and judgment I could place confidence.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d189-a1.xml" xpointer="d189-a1"/>
            </div>
